@participant3  @participant2 Unfortunately, even on the latest, it still happens...note it working on VIP 240.240.179.**_184_**, then starting to blackhole, then coming back online on 240.240.179._**182**_.

![image](https://github.com/istio/istio/assets/69006307/9631482b-d8a8-4701-9ad8-230c5cabc595)

What would cause Istio to push new auto-allocated IP's when using `ISTIO_META_DNS_AUTO_ALLOCATE: "true"`? Unfortunately, even though turning this off "fixes" the issue, we can't; it introduced the issue it was meant to fix, which is proxying TCP traffic for 2 different `ServiceEntries` on the same port, to different URL's. In this case, it's an AWS Postgres instance with a reader and writer replica.
